    {
      "id": "ZBYS",
      "code_hash": "bb91c887bedac4a85dd0e4a2493e57b2",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h3 id=\"model-context-protocol\">Model Context Protocol</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">MCP enables agents to:</span>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Access live, external data</strong> from databases, APIS, and\nservices without custom integration code</li>\n<li><strong>Leverage community-built tools</strong> with standardized\ninterfaces</li>\n<li><strong>Scale capabilities</strong> by connecting to multiple\nspecialized servers</li>\n</ul></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "aLJB",
      "code_hash": "03b7dd734007cfdc10cdaf772a053d84",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h3 id=\"how-mcp-works\">How MCP Works</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">MCP connects your agent (the <strong>client</strong>) to the\nexternal <strong>MCP servers</strong> that provide tools:</span>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>MCP Server</strong>: Provides specific tools (like image\ngeneration, database access etc...)</li>\n<li><strong>MCP Client</strong>: Your agent that uses those tools</li>\n<li><strong>All servers work the same way</strong> - standardized\ninterface</li>\n</ul></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "nHfw",
      "code_hash": "33a55e6a34e6de642bf07433fb61f1b1",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h3 id=\"mcp-workflow\">MCP workflow</h3>\n<ol>\n<li>Choose an MCP Server and tool</li>\n<li>Create the MCP Toolset (configure connection)</li>\n<li>Add it to your agent</li>\n<li>Run and test the agent</li>\n</ol>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">For demo purposes we'll use <a href=\"https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/servers/tree/main/src/everything\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Evyerthing MCP Server</a></span>\n<ul>\n<li>an npm packaged designed to testing MCP integrations.</li>\n</ul>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">We will used <code>getTinyImage</code> tool to return a simple test\nimage (16x16 pixels, Base64-encoded).</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">For prod you would use servers for Google Maps, Slack, Discord\netc...</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
